  "readmeFile": "PACKAGE.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Conformance: non-streaming type/serialization correctness and more streaming breadth. fn:available-system-properties now returns a sequence of xs:QName (was a single non-QName item, failing binding to xs:QName*). A variable/parameter/function with as=\"ATOMIC-TYPE\" and a temporary-tree or node-valued body now atomizes and casts to the declared atomic type (date/time/duration/anyURI/untypedAtomic/etc.) instead of leaving a raw result-tree-fragment — node-typed as= keeps its nodes. Invalid xsl:output / xsl:result-document / disable-output-escaping values now raise XTSE0020 instead of being silently ignored. Streaming: a streamed xsl:copy / copy-of preserves in-scope namespace declarations and prefixes; xsl:for-each whose select is a conditional (if(…) then … else …) streams the selected branch; a wildcard-attribute existence climb (ancestor::*/@*) streams; and a consuming attribute sequence (data(@x)) atomizes correctly in a streamed copy. Requires PhoenixmlDb.Core 1.2.2 and PhoenixmlDb.XQuery 1.5.4. No API changes. See RELEASES.md for full notes.",
